\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Top view of the two-radar setup. $f_C$ carries $V_x$ (speed), $f_\Delta $ carries $V_z$ (azimuth $\alpha $ in the $x$--$z$ plane). The factor $2L/b$ corrects the parallax: the farther the ball, the smaller the frequency difference for the same $V_z$.}}{36}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces The aluminium patch as a single dominant scatterer. Both the flash periodicity and the spectral excursion measure the \emph {total} spin $\omega $; neither separates backspin from sidespin.}}{37}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Python validation pipeline (\texttt {sci/pipe\_validation.py}). Scilab equivalents: \texttt {animDensite} (STFT), \texttt {Info}/\texttt {GetSwing} (speed), \texttt {animHilbert} (envelope), \texttt {acos(f2/f1)} (rudimentary azimuth in \texttt {testsFFT.sci}).}}{39}{}%
